*Heisenberg Uncertainty Principle:* The uncertainty (standard deviation) of position $sigma_x$ and momentum $sigma_p$ are bounded such that their product has a fundamental lower limit. This reflects the wave-particle duality and limits the precision of simultaneous measurements.
